# Why promote abstractions to utils

`@pixel-forge/utils` exists so general TypeScript helpers are not rewritten
in every library. A function that only happened to be born in `log` or
another package still belongs on the matching utils subpath once it is a
named helper.

`isPlainObject` started on `BrowserLogger` to tell `typeof === 'object'`
from real objects (`null`, arrays, `Error`, `Date`, `RegExp`). That is not
a logger concern; it belongs in `@pixel-forge/utils/object`.

This sits after specify-then-abstract and extract-second-copy: implement
the specified behavior locally, extract when a second site needs it, then
promote if the helper has no package domain. Do not mint a utils helper
in the same change that first needs the behavior.
